# Root Docker build-context exclusions (requirements/63) — used when a service's
# Dockerfile needs the repo root as context (e.g. mathbank-rest/Dockerfile.lambda, to
# reach the sibling mathbank-geometry-engine dependency). Mirrors .gitignore's heavy
# directories plus a few Docker-specific ones; without this file, `docker build .` from
# the repo root would try to send the entire multi-GB working tree (archive/,
# mathbank-data-ingestion/data/, every .venv/node_modules) to the Docker daemon.
.git/
archive/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/*.egg-info/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.eggs/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/
mathbank-data-ingestion/data/
mathbank-data-ingestion/data_textbook/
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/cdk.out/
# CRITICAL: never let real secrets into a Docker build context/image layer (found live,
# requirements/63, GOTCHAS.md #43 — mathbank-agent's Dockerfile.lambda copied its whole
# directory, including the real .env, straight into the image before this exclusion
# existed). Lambda functions get their config from real environment variables (set by
# CDK, some fetched from SSM at cold start) — a .env file should never be present inside
# any container image, local test or deployed, for any service.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
